      "writtenOn": "2022-11-30T18:03:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Since the PCT sensors are on i2c, I believe we\u0027d expect to see an i2c error a the time of a sensor read failure.  \n\nHowever, the driver caches its reads once per second for the thermal-related hooks to use.  So for this specific call, we\u0027ll only ever get a success accessing the cache, or an unpowered error if the sensor isn\u0027t on right now.  Or an invalid error if we just sent it an invalid sensor to access.  That one might be worth logging since it would be a coding error",
      "parentUuid": "36a918f2_1445cabd",
      "revId": "336fb10300c44db77700b02cbce5737678a2675c",
      "serverId": "3ce6091f-6c88-37e8-8c75-72f92ae8dfba"
    },
